# .dockerignore — keeps the build context minimal and, critically, keeps
# secrets and host-only artifacts out of the image (docs/20-Dockerization.md
# §2/§9). This is the actual enforcement mechanism behind "never bake a
# credential into the image" — not just a documented convention.

.git/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
reports/*
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.vscode/
.idea/
test-results/
playwright-report/
.playwright/
